## Quick‑Start: Add “Sign in with Google” to Your Bolt‑Supabase App  

> **Who is this for?**  
> You’ve built a simple front‑end with Bolt (or any vanilla‑JS front‑end) and you’re using Supabase for authentication & data. You’re not a heavy developer and want a step‑by‑step guide that works out‑of‑the‑box.

---

### 1️⃣ Prerequisites

| What you need | How to get it |
|---------------|---------------|
| **Supabase Project** | 👉 [Create one](https://app.supabase.com/)  
| **Bolt** | 👉 Use the Starter Kit from [Boost](https://boost.geekycode.com/) or simply link Bolt CDN in your HTML `<script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@bodiless/bolt/dist/bolt.min.js"></script>` |
| **Google Cloud Console Account** | 👉 Create a project at https://console.cloud.google.com/ |

---

### 2️⃣ Set Up Google Sign‑In in Supabase

1. **Open your Supabase dashboard**  
   → `Authentication` → `Settings` → `External OAuth Providers`.

2. **Click “Enable” next to Google**.

3. **Fill out the form**  

   | Field | Value |
   |-------|-------|
   | **Client ID** | From Google Cloud (see step 3) |
   | **Client Secret** | From Google Cloud |
   | **Redirect URLs** | `http://localhost:3000` (or your production URL) |
   | **Scopes** | `openid profile email` (default) |

4. **Save**.

---

### 3️⃣ Create OAuth Credentials in Google Cloud

1. Go to the [Google Cloud Console](https://console.cloud.google.com/).
2. Create a **new Project** (or choose an existing one).
3. In the left menu → **APIs & Services** → **OAuth consent screen** →  
   • Set “External” user type (free tier 👍)  
   • Fill in required fields → **Save and Continue**.  
4. In **Credentials** → **Create Credentials** → **OAuth 2.0 Client ID**:  
   • Application type: *Web application*  
   • Authorized redirect URI: `http://localhost:3000` (or your domain)  
   • Click *Create*  

5. Copy the **Client ID** and **Client Secret** to the Supabase form (step 2).

---

### 4️⃣ Hook it up in Bolt

Below is a minimal example.  
Put this in your `index.html` (or any JS file that runs on page load).

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <title>Bolt + Supabase – Google Sign‑In</title>
  <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@supabase/supabase-js@2"></script>
  <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/@bodiless/bolt/dist/bolt.min.js"></script>
</head>
<body>

  <div id="auth">
    <button id="login">Sign in with Google</button>
    <button id="logout" style="display:none;">Sign out</button>
    <p id="status"></p>
  </div>

  <script>
    // 1️⃣ Init Supabase
    const supabaseUrl = 'https://<YOUR-PROJECT>.supabase.co';
    const supabaseKey = '<YOUR-ANON-KEY>';
    const supabase = supabase.createClient(supabaseUrl, supabaseKey);

    // 2️⃣ Helpers
    const loginBtn  = document.getElementById('login');
    const logoutBtn = document.getElementById('logout');
    const status    = document.getElementById('status');

    async function showUser(user) {
      if(user) {
        status.textContent = `🧑‍🚀 Welcome, ${user.email}`;
        loginBtn.style.display = 'none';
        logoutBtn.style.display = 'inline';
      } else {
        status.textContent = '🔐 Please sign in';
        loginBtn.style.display = 'inline';
        logoutBtn.style.display = 'none';
      }
    }

    // 3️⃣ Sign‑in route
    loginBtn.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      const { error } = await supabase.auth.signInWithOAuth({
        provider: 'google',
      });
      if (error) {
        console.error(error);
        alert('Sign‑in failed');
      }
    });

    // 4️⃣ Sign‑out
    logoutBtn.addEventListener('click', async () => {
      await supabase.auth.signOut();
    });

    // 5️⃣ Persist auth state across refreshes
    supabase.auth.getSession().then(({ data: { session } }) => {
      showUser(session?.user ?? null);
    });

    // 6️⃣ Listen for auth changes
    supabase.auth.onAuthStateChange((_event, session) => {
      showUser(session?.user ?? null);
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
```

#### 🎉 What this does

- Button shows “Sign in with Google” → triggers a Supabase OAuth flow.  
- After successful login, user is redirected back to your page.  
- The UI updates to show the email and a “Sign out” button.  

---

### 5️⃣ Test it

1. **Run a local server** (e.g. `npx http-server .` or `python -m http.server`).  
2. Navigate to `http://localhost:3000`.  
3. Click **Sign in with Google** → complete Google flow → you should see your email.

---

### 6️⃣ Deploy

If you’re using Vercel, Netlify, or similar:
- Add the same `supabaseUrl` & `supabaseKey` for your production project.  
- Ensure the redirect URL in Supabase & Google matches your deployed domain.  
- No server‑side code is needed.

---

## Optional Extras (Nice to Have)

| Feature | Why? | Quick Tip |
|---------|------|-----------|
| **Email** | To send welcome emails or password‑reset links | Supabase Auth > Settings > Email |
| **Profile Picture** | Friendly UI | `user.user_metadata.avatar_url` |
| **Session Timeout** | Security | Supabase Auth > Settings > Session |
| **Custom Sign‑In Page** | Branding | Replace the button with your own UI, keep the `supabase.auth.signInWithOAuth` call. |

---

**Finished!**  
You now have “Sign in with Google” working with Bolt and Supabase, without writing any backend code. 🎉

Feel free to ask if you hit any snags or want to add extra features!
